"id": "subjunctive",
"el": "Η υποτακτική: να, ας, μη(ν)",
"title": "The subjunctive: να, ας and μη(ν)",
"span": "A2–B1",
"blurb": "Greek has no infinitive: \"I want to go\" is θέλω να πάω. How να works with both aspects, which verbs take να + present, negating with μη(ν), the free-standing να of wishes and offers, ας \"let's\", and για να / χωρίς να / αντί να.",
"intro": [
{
"p": "Modern Greek lost its infinitive. Where English says \"to go\", Greek says **να πάω** \"that I go\", with a full personal ending: **θέλω να πάω** \"I want to go\", **θέλω να πας** \"I want you to go\". This **να** form (the subjunctive) is one of the most used structures in the language."
},
